{"id": "114684", "revid": "38175", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=114684", "title": "Yabelo", "text": "Yabelo is in the Oromia region of southern Ethiopia. The town's name is spelled in many different ways, Yabello, Yavello, Iavello or Yebelo, and an alternative name is Obda, which is also the name of a nearby mountain. Yabelo is located at a latitude and longitude of 4\u00b053\u2032N 38\u00b05\u2032E and an elevation of 1857 meters above sea level. \nUnderstand.\nYabelo is a small town with two gas stations, telephone service, a post office and a commercial bank, as well as at least one primary and one secondary school. \nGet in.\nYabelo is located close to the main road from Addis Ababa to the border with Kenya, which is part of the Trans African Highway 4 (TAH4), from Cairo to Cape Town. Bus connections exist from Addis Ababa and from the border town of Moyale."}
{"id": "114731", "revid": "2253620", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=114731", "title": "Schull", "text": "Schull (pronounced \"skull\") is a harbour town on the Mizen Head peninsula of County Cork, at the southwest tip of Ireland. The name means school, and was first documented in 1199 suggesting a religious seminary, but there's no trace of that. Once a fishing port, Schull is now a tourist resort, with a population in 2022 of 669. \nMizen Head is the tip of the peninsula that for many emigrants was their last sight of Ireland. It's the most southerly of three that form a claw on the country's foot, and its villages and sights are described here. Sheep's Head is the middle peninsula, described on the page for Bantry, and Beara the northern peninsula is described under Glengarriff and Castletownbere.\nGet in.\nBy road follow N71 from Cork and turn off at Ballydehob.\nBus Eireann 237 runs daily from Cork via Bandon, Clonakilty, Rosscarbery and Skibbereen. There the service branches, with three buses continuing to Ballydehob and Schull, 2 hr 15 min altogether, and two persevere as far west as Goleen. The other buses turn south at Skibbereen to Baltimore.\nOn Tuesday and Friday mornings a Local Link bus runs from Goleen via Schull and Durrus to Bantry, returning early afternoon; you need to book on +353 27 52727. \n is the bus stop in Schull, next to Bunratty Inn.\nFerries to Cape Clear sail from Schull harbour June-Aug 3-6 days a week. The ferry to Cape Clear from Baltimore is year-round. \n is the pier for the ferry to Long Island. It sails daily around 9AM and 5PM and takes 5 min.\nGet around.\nYou need wheels to explore the peninsula. \nNo local taxi, it would have to come from Skibbereen.\n What's on? - see the Town of Schull website.\nConnect.\nAs of August 2025, Schull and its approach roads have 4G from Eir, and 5G from Three and Vodafone."}
{"id": "114750", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=114750", "title": "Lake Macquarie", "text": "Lake Macquarie is a satellite city of Newcastle with the largest permanent saltwater lake in the Southern Hemisphere. It is a contemporary coastal city and natural adventure playground.\nUnderstand.\nThe City of Lake Macquarie is often considered part of its immediate neighbour, Newcastle, but is in fact a separate city with a much larger area and a population of 214,000 (2021). It has a number of suburbs including:\nGet in.\nIt is easiest to get to Lake Macquarie by car. Take the Pacific Motorway (M1) from Sydney or the Central Coast.\nThe closest airfield is Lake Macquarie Airfield.\nThe closest airport is Newcastle Airport, which is itself half an hour north from Newcastle, meaning a one-hour drive from the airport.\nBy train.\nLake Macquarie is not directly connected to the main train line running parallel to it on the other side of the actual Lake itself. Wyee train station is closest in proximity to the Morisset area, whilst Fassifern is popular amongst those travelling into Toronto. There is no track on the eastern side. However, there used to be a line between Belmont and Adamstown, which is now a popular rail trail (Fernleigh Track).\nGet around.\nA car is your best option for getting around, although many people use the area for cycling.\nBy bus.\nInformation on buses for the Lake Macquarie area are available from the Lake Macquarie City Council website."}
{"id": "114754", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=114754", "title": "Lyons (Colorado)", "text": "Lyons is in Colorado.\nUnderstand.\nLyons is a Statutory Town in Boulder County, Colorado, United States. \nGet in.\nFly in to Denver, Take Pena to E-470 West (toll road) to I-25 North to 66 West past Longmont.\nGet around.\nWalk, drive, ride the bus- It is a pretty small town, only 1.2 square miles or 3.108 square kilometers.\nSee.\nRedstone Museum, Rockygrass Festival, Lyons Outdoor Games.\nDo.\nKayak, Hike, Mountain Bike, Fish.\nBuy.\nBikes, Antiques.\nRed Sandstone\nEat.\nOskar Blues, Smokin' Daves, The Barking Dog Cafe, The Stone Cup Cafe, Nepal's Cafe, Lyons Dairy Bar, The Old ChubWay, The Fork, Dave's Diner, Julie's Thai, The Soda Fountain.\nDrink.\nOskar Blues, The Soda Fountain.\nSleep.\nSteamboat Mountain Lodge, Aspen Leaf Motel, Ferg's Inn. \nConnect.\nhttp://townoflyons.com\nPhone: +1 303-823-6622\n432 5th Ave, PO Box 49\nGo next.\nRocky Mountain National Park, Estes Park, Allen's Park, Nederland, Boulder, Longmont, Denver."}
