{"id": "120143", "revid": "2236161", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=120143", "title": "Williamsburg (Kentucky)", "text": "Williamsburg is a small city in Kentucky's Daniel Boone Country.\nUnderstand.\nWilliamsburg is the county seat of Whitley County and is home to the University of the Cumberlands, a private university affiliated with the Southern Baptist Church.\nGet in.\nThe city is situated on I-75 just north of the Tennessee border.\nDrink.\nAlcohol sales are allowed by the drink in restaurants that seat at least 100 people. The nearest towns that allow package sales are Corbin, about 15 minutes' drive to the north, and Jellico, about the same distance to the south and just over the Tennessee border."}
